      "zh-Hans": { title: "海外网红营销｜跨境创作者合作与项目管理 | 榛果营销", description: "海外网红营销的市场选择、本地沟通、寄样、审核、付款与内容授权管理。", h1: "海外网红营销：先选对市场，再安排创作者合作", answer: "跨境创作者合作的难点不在翻译，而在市场选择、本地内容语境、寄样、付款、审核与授权协调。榛果会先拆清单一市场的目标和限制，再规划创作者与排期；没有可验证的海外结果时，不会用台湾案例替代。", sections: [["先做市场判断", ["按产品可寄送性、语言资源、本地承接页和售后能力筛选市场。", "进入新市场通常先用单一国家测试内容和流程，再判断是否扩大。", "同一脚本不能直接复制到不同市场，使用情境、合规说法和内容习惯不同。"]], ["跨境项目增加的工作", ["寄样前确认地址格式、物流限制、产品成分和通关风险。", "付款、汇率、文件和税务处理须按合作对象与市场另行确认。", "翻译不等于本地化；brief 既要保留品牌限制，也要给创作者自然表达空间。"]], ["时间与风险管理", ["将回复、寄样到货、初稿、修改与上线排成可追踪节点。", "提前确认标示、使用权、竞品限制和素材投放需求，避免发布后重谈。", "卖点、承接页或客服未准备好时，不适合直接多国同步。"]], ["品牌需要准备", ["可供当地使用的产品说明、成分或规格、禁用说法与图片素材。", "目标市场、平台、预算、最晚上线日和可接受内容形式。", "当地法律、税务、海关和广告标示应由当地专业单位确认。"]]], faqs: [["海外网红营销应先做一国还是多国？", "没有海外验证时，先做一国更容易控制寄样、内容与承接页，再决定是否扩大。"], ["为什么海外项目周期更长？", "多了本地沟通、寄送、回复、付款与多方审核，不能只按本地发帖排期估算。"], ["哪些产品不适合直接做海外合作？", "不能寄样、产品说明不完整、当地承接与客服未准备好，或无法处理必要标示的产品，应先补足基础。"]], cta: "讨论目标市场" },
      en: { title: "Overseas Influencer Marketing | Cross-Border Creator Campaigns | Zhenguo", description: "Market selection, local communication, product seeding, review, payment, and usage-rights coordination for cross-border creator work.", h1: "Overseas influencer marketing starts with market choice, not a translated brief", answer: "The difficult part of cross-border creator work is coordinating market choice, local content context, seeding, payments, review, and rights, not translating copy. Zhenguo defines one market's goal and constraints before planning creators and timing; Taiwan results are never presented as overseas proof.", sections: [["Choose the market first", ["Screen markets by product shippability, language support, local landing pages, and customer service readiness.", "For a new market, a single-country test usually produces clearer learning than simultaneous multi-country activity.", "Do not reuse one script unchanged across markets: usage context, claims, and creator conventions vary."]], ["What cross-border work adds", ["Confirm address formats, shipping restrictions, ingredients, and customs risks before seeding.", "Payment, foreign exchange, documents, and tax treatment must be confirmed by market and counterparty.", "Translation is not localization; a brief must protect brand constraints while leaving room for natural creator expression."]], ["Timing and risk", ["Track creator reply, delivery, draft, revision, and publishing as separate milestones.", "Set disclosure, rights, exclusivity, and paid-media expectations before content is made.", "Do not launch multi-country work before product claims, landing pages, and local customer support are ready."]], ["What brands should prepare", ["Market-ready product information, specifications, restricted claims, and approved visual assets.", "Target market, channel, budget, latest launch date, and acceptable formats.", "Local legal, tax, customs, and advertising requirements should be confirmed with local specialists."]]], faqs: [["Should we start with one market or several?", "Without proven overseas operations, one market is easier to control across seeding, content, and the landing experience."], ["Why do overseas projects take longer?", "Local communication, delivery, response times, payment, and multi-party review add work beyond a local posting schedule."], ["Which products are not ready for overseas creator work?", "Products that cannot be seeded, lack complete information, lack local support, or cannot meet required disclosures should be prepared first."]], cta: "Discuss a target market" }
